---
import { RESOURCE_LIMITS } from '../lib/plans';
---
<ul class="rules">
  <li><strong>Quotas count what your organization creates:</strong> posts, comments and uploads. Paid plans reset every UTC calendar month. The free start is one-time and never resets.</li>
  <li><strong>A scheduled post counts when you create it</strong> (or move it out of draft), not when it publishes, so you can schedule ahead as far as your quota allows.</li>
  <li><strong>Drafts are free.</strong> A post starts counting when it leaves <code>DRAFT</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>Checked once.</strong> Quotas and caps are checked when you create or schedule. A scheduled post is never refused later because of a quota.</li>
  <li><strong>Retries are free.</strong> A failed post can be retried up to {RESOURCE_LIMITS.maxRetries} times without counting again.</li>
  <li><strong>Daily caps</strong> count posts and comments aimed at one connected account on one UTC day. They follow the account on the network, so disconnecting and reconnecting, or adding it to another brand, does not reset them.</li>
  <li><strong>Media</strong> is kept for {RESOURCE_LIMITS.mediaRetentionDays} days after its last use. Published posts on the networks are never affected.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage is readable any time</strong> from <code>GET /organization/usage/posts</code>, <code>/comments</code>, <code>/uploads</code>, <code>/daily-limits</code> and <code>/imports</code>.</li>
</ul>
<style>.rules li { margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: var(--fs-15); }</style>
